# House style rules that CI enforces.
#
# This is a copy. The canonical version lives in the resilience-resources
# repository, which is where most of the writing happens. The weekly
# external links workflow checks this copy still matches it, so the two
# cannot drift apart without somebody being told.
#
# Kept here rather than inside the checker so that the rules are data a
# contributor can read and propose changes to, and so that the file doing
# the enforcing does not have to contain the words it rejects.
#
# These apply to everything in the repository, prose and source alike. A rule
# about how we write is not suspended inside a docstring, a comment or a
# button label.
#
# One rule per line, as "text = why". Lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# To exempt a line that has to contain a banned word, a test fixture
# demonstrating the rule for instance, put "house-style: allow" in a comment
# on that line.

quietly = house style
genuinely = house style
honest = house style, and honestly, honesty, dishonest with it
— = em dash, use a comma or a full stop or rewrite the sentence
